        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Antiviral drug development faces a core challenge: viruses use host machinery for\nmost steps of replication. Selectively targeting the virus without harming the host\nrequires identifying virus-specific targets. The major classes of antivirals map\ndirectly onto stages of the replication cycle."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-ANTIVIRAL-STRATEGIES.md#003",
      "path": [
        "07-ANTIVIRAL-STRATEGIES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:virology:07-antiviral-strategies, git-history:virology:07-antiviral-strategies]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/07-ANTIVIRAL-STRATEGIES.md",
        "concepts": "[antiviral, strategies]",
        "current_path": "virology/07-ANTIVIRAL-STRATEGIES.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:antiviral-strategies",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[antiviral, strategies]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Antiviral Drugs and Resistance Mechanisms",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│               ANTIVIRAL TARGET MAP                               │\n│                                                                  │\n│  REPLICATION STEP          DRUG CLASS            TARGET EXAMPLES │\n│  ─────────────────         ──────────            ─────────────── │\n│  Attachment                Entry inhibitors      Maraviroc (HIV) │\n│  Membrane fusion           Fusion inhibitors     Enfuvirtide     │\n│  Genome release            Capsid inhibitors     Lenacapavir     │\n│  Viral polymerase          NRTIs/NNRTIs/NAs      AZT, Sofosbuvir │\n│  RNA replication           RdRp inhibitors       Remdesivir      │\n│  Protease cleavage         Protease inhibitors   Lopinavir,      │\n│                                                   Nirmatrelvir   │\n│  Integrase                 INSTIs                Dolutegravir    │\n│  Neuraminidase             NA inhibitors         Oseltamivir     │\n│  Capsid assembly           Capsid assembly inhib.Lenacapavir     │\n│  Nuclear export            Cap-snatching inhib.  Baloxavir (flu) │\n│  Immune evasion block      IFN inducers          Type I IFN      │\n│                                                                  │\n│  GENERAL PRINCIPLE: virus-specific enzymes are the best targets  │\n│  (no host counterpart = selective toxicity)                      │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```"
    },
