      "text": "### Mechanism"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-ANTIVIRAL-STRATEGIES.md#008",
      "path": [
        "07-ANTIVIRAL-STRATEGIES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:virology:07-antiviral-strategies, git-history:virology:07-antiviral-strategies]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/07-ANTIVIRAL-STRATEGIES.md",
        "concepts": "[antiviral, strategies]",
        "current_path": "virology/07-ANTIVIRAL-STRATEGIES.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:antiviral-strategies",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[antiviral, strategies]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Antiviral Drugs and Resistance Mechanisms",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  NUCLEOSIDE ANALOG MECHANISM:\n  ──────────────────────────────\n  1. Drug (modified nucleoside) enters cell\n  2. Phosphorylated by cellular kinases to triphosphate form\n     (NRTIs need 3 phosphorylations; NtRTIs come pre-phosphorylated at 1 level)\n  3. Viral polymerase incorporates the analog instead of natural nucleotide\n  4. Chain termination: missing 3'-OH prevents next nucleotide addition\n     OR mutagenic incorporation: altered base pairing → mutation accumulation\n     OR active site blockade"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-ANTIVIRAL-STRATEGIES.md#009",
      "path": [
        "07-ANTIVIRAL-STRATEGIES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:virology:07-antiviral-strategies, git-history:virology:07-antiviral-strategies]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/07-ANTIVIRAL-STRATEGIES.md",
        "concepts": "[antiviral, strategies]",
        "current_path": "virology/07-ANTIVIRAL-STRATEGIES.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:antiviral-strategies",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[antiviral, strategies]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Antiviral Drugs and Resistance Mechanisms",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "KEY: Viral polymerases often have different structural/kinetic properties\n  from host DNA polymerases → some analogs are preferentially incorporated\n  by viral enzymes → selectivity\n```"
    },
