        "root_concepts": "[antiviral, strategies]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Antiviral Drugs and Resistance Mechanisms",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  HIV (NRTIs — Nucleoside RT Inhibitors):\n  ─────────────────────────────────────────\n  Zidovudine (AZT, ZDV): thymidine analog; chain terminator\n                           First approved antiretroviral (1987)\n                           Resistance: M184V, TAMs (thymidine analog mutations)\n  Lamivudine (3TC): cytidine analog; well-tolerated; also active vs. HBV\n                    Resistance: M184V (emerges rapidly; reduces viral fitness)\n  Tenofovir (TDF/TAF): adenosine analog; nucleotide (pre-phosphorylated at one level)\n                       Backbone of current HIV regimens; also first-line HBV\n                       Resistance: K65R (rare; compromises RT processivity)\n  Emtricitabine (FTC): cytidine analog; similar to 3TC; combined with tenofovir\n  Abacavir (ABC): guanosine analog; HLA-B*57:01 screening required (hypersensitivity)"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-ANTIVIRAL-STRATEGIES.md#012",
      "path": [
        "07-ANTIVIRAL-STRATEGIES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:virology:07-antiviral-strategies, git-history:virology:07-antiviral-strategies]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/07-ANTIVIRAL-STRATEGIES.md",
