        "root_concepts": "[antiviral, strategies]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Antiviral Drugs and Resistance Mechanisms",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "SARS-CoV-2 / other RNA viruses (RdRp inhibitors):\n  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  Remdesivir (GS-5734): adenosine analog; chain terminator for RdRp\n                         Active vs. SARS-CoV-2, Ebola, RSV (broad spectrum)\n                         Mechanism: incorporated by nsp12 RdRp → terminates\n                         strand extension 3 nucleotides after incorporation\n                         (\"delayed chain terminator\" — bypasses ExoN proofreading)\n                         Modest clinical benefit in COVID-19 (IV formulation)"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-ANTIVIRAL-STRATEGIES.md#013",
      "path": [
